+    """`bi $rN` sites whose target is a constant: the nearest write to rN in
+    the same chunk, with no branch, call or stop between, is an `il`/`ila`.
+
+    That is how Sony's SPU code moves between the halves of an interrupt
+    window -- `ila $r3,<resume> / bid $r3` -- and it is most of the indirect
+    transfers in WWS job modules. Lifted as an indirect transfer, each goes
+    back to the drain loop, through spu_indirect_branch and a registry lookup,
+    to land on an address known at lift time. A chunk starts at every branch
+    target, so nothing enters between the load and the branch. Returns
+    {bi addr: target}. (Ported from the MotorStorm Apocalypse port's lifter.)"""
